-- the interconversions of a set of forms, each with its half-life in minutes; zero where there is
-- none. Thalidomide is the case that makes this necessary: the stereocentre inverts in human serum
-- with a half-life of about 22 minutes for the (S) form and 33 for the (R), so the two enantiomers are
-- not two substances that stay apart, and the claim that the (R) form is safe is a claim about a point
